 arm as the Italian tried to touch the finishing board, and Muller was disqualified, giving Bruni the silver medal. This gave bronze to Brazil’s " [:a {:href ""} "Poliana Okimota"] ", two seconds behind second, but 23 seconds ahead of fourth-placed " [:a {:href "/athletes/122340"} "Xin Xin"] " of China."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Lap 1"] [:th {} "Lap 2"] [:th {} "Lap 3"] [:th {} "Lap 2 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 3 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 4 Split"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125722"} "Sharon van Rouwendaal"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "1-56:32.1"] [:td {} "30:53.1 (12)"] [:td {} "1-01:00.2 (6)"] [:td {} "1-29:29.5 (5)"] [:td {} "30:07.1 (11)"] [:td {} "28:29.3 (2)"] [:td {} "27:02.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130687"} "Rachele Bruni"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "1-56:49.5"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "1-01:04.0 (11)"] [:td {} "1-29:33.4 (6)"] [:td {} "28:29.4 (1)"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "27:16.1 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "No reason was given, but Official Results and MyInfo2016 only contained splits for some of the female open water swimmers.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116005"} "Poliana Okimoto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-ali